    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="0561" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1301</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-09T23:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1917—11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Delgado, a congressman, with four other important rebel chiefs, and 400
                    men surrendered to Government at Arroyo Blanco, Camaguey Province today. Some
                    soldiers who deserted at Camaguey at inception revolt are among these men.
                    Surrender regarded as most important by the Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
